## Generate from an example mobile app

An example mobile app declares the API task in `Codepotg.yaml`:

```yaml
tasks:
  api:
    input: ../backend/dev/openapi/v1/openapi.v1.yaml
    language: dart
    templateDir: ../backend/dev/templates/dart
    output: ./pkg/api
```

Run the app's normal Codepot `api` task. It compiles the backend OpenAPI file,
renders this package into `pkg/api`, resolves Dart dependencies, runs
`build_runner`, formats the package, and refreshes the Flutter app dependencies.

## Post-generation validation

From the generated package:

```bash
cd pkg/api
flutter pub get
dart run build_runner build --delete-conflicting-outputs
dart format --output=none --set-exit-if-changed lib
flutter analyze
flutter test
```

The backend also provides a validator for an already generated app package:

```bash
CODEPOTG_APP_DIR=../example_app pnpm openapi:validate:dart-runtime
```

Use another fictional app path when validating a second client. The validator reads
`<app>/Codepotg.yaml` and validates `<app>/pkg/api`; it does not incorrectly
expect `codepot-openapi generate` to emit a Dart package inside the backend.

Verify the generated application imports only this package and all generated
operations carry stable operation IDs.
